","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-08-29T21:28:49Z","updated_at":"2019-08-29T21:29:32Z","body":"Wow, that's an amazingly quick fix!\r\n\r\nThe issue arose because some application stores data in multiple (three) SQLite files, which I am working against. I thought I should include all these in the same session. There are some table columns corresponding between the different files. Is that what \"vertical\" means? (Sorry, I am very new to SQLAlchemy.)\r\n\r\nPerhaps an easier approach in my case is to create separate sessions for the individual databases? The cte doesn't span multiple databases anyway. (And yeah, I'm mostly just toying around so a solution that uses `binds` would be neat, but is by no means necessary.)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/526369652/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"wpk-","id":4181003,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxODEwMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4181003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-","html_url":"https://github.com/wpk-","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/526371321","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4829#issuecomment-526371321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4829","id":526371321,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyNjM3MTMyMQ==","user":{"login":"wpk-","id":4181003,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxODEwMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4181003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-","html_url":"https://github.com/wpk-","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-08-29T21:34:31Z","updated_at":"2019-08-29T21:34:31Z","body":"(PS. I would multiply `parts_alias.quantity` by `incl_alias.c.quantity`  in the `included_parts.union_all` statement.)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/526371321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"wpk-","id":4181003,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxODEwMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4181003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-","html_url":"https://github.com/wpk-","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wpk-/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/526374987","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4829#issuecomment-526374987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4829","id":526374987,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyNjM3NDk4Nw==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-08-29T21:47:01Z","updated_at":"2019-08-29T21:47:01Z","body":"\"vertical\" means that yes, you have the total set of data you are dealing with partioned among multiple databases, and the databases are split what we say \"veritcally\", that is, different tables are in different databases.    If the split was \"horizontal\" then you'd have different rows of a single table in the different databases.\r\n\r\nfor your use case, using one Session is indeed a fairly reasonable way to do it, however, if you want to use multiple sessions instead, that is fine as well.     A workaround you can do for now is to populate the \"binds\" dictionary with all the Table objects you care about also.     this is not super convenient, but if you can make sure that you've mapped all your classes first, you can use a recipe like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\nbinds = {Base: engine}\r\nbinds.update({table: engine for table in Base.metadata.tables.values()})\r\n\r\nSession = sessionmaker(binds=binds)\r\n\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/526374987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issu